-- title:
--   Weight-two cusp forms form a cyclic Hecke module
-- statement:
--   Let $N$ be a nonzero natural number, and let $S_2(\Gamma_0(N))$ denote the complex vector space `CuspForm (CongruenceSubgroup.Gamma0 N) 2` of weight-two cusp forms for $\Gamma_0(N)$. Write $\mathbb{T}$ for [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 ∅`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18), the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb{C}}\, S_2(\Gamma_0(N))$ generated by the set consisting of the operators [`CuspForm.heckeTLin`](def/ModularForm_HeckeOperatorForms.html#L69) attached to primes $\ell$ not dividing $N$ together with the operators [`CuspForm.heckeULin`](def/ModularForm_HeckeOperatorForms.html#L83) attached to primes $q$ dividing $N$ (the third argument, the set of primes to be omitted from the generating set, being empty, so that no prime is omitted). The assertion is that there exists a cusp form $f \in S_2(\Gamma_0(N))$ such that for every $g \in S_2(\Gamma_0(N))$ there is an endomorphism $T$ lying in the $\mathbb{C}$-linear span, inside $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb{C}}\, S_2(\Gamma_0(N))$, of the underlying set of $\mathbb{T}$, with $T f = g$. Thus $S_2(\Gamma_0(N))$ is a cyclic module over the complex algebra spanned by the Hecke operators $T_\ell$ ($\ell \nmid N$) and $U_q$ ($q \mid N$), with generator $f$.
--
--   This is the cyclicity (multiplicity-one, or Gorenstein-type) statement for the full Hecke algebra acting on weight-two cusp forms of level $\Gamma_0(N)$, obtained from a decomposition of the space into rescaled newform lines separated by their Hecke eigenvalues. It is used in the construction of a distinguished generator of the Hecke module, in [`CuspForm.exists_top_eq_heckeAlgebra_adjoin_smul`](thm.html#CuspForm.exists_top_eq_heckeAlgebra_adjoin_smul) and [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra_adjoin_exists_frobenius_form`](thm.html#CuspForm.heckeAlgebra_adjoin_exists_frobenius_form).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CuspForm_exists_cyclic_span_heckeAlgebra.lean

import Definitions.Def_CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

theorem CuspForm.exists_cyclic_span_heckeAlgebra (N : ℕ) [NeZero N] :
    ∃ f : CuspForm (CongruenceSubgroup.Gamma0 N) 2,
      ∀ g : CuspForm (CongruenceSubgroup.Gamma0 N) 2,
        ∃ T ∈ Submodule.span ℂ (CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 (∅ : Set ℕ) : Set (Module.End ℂ (CuspForm (CongruenceSubgroup.Gamma0 N) 2))),
          T f = g := by sorry
